#: ../../../moving_robot.md:1
msgid "Moving the robot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:3
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to move our robot. We will use the robot "
"we built in the [Build your own robot](building_robot) tutorial. You can "
"download the robot from [here](https://github.com/ignitionrobotics/docs/blob/"
"master/fortress/tutorials/building_robot/building_robot.sdf). You can also "
"find the finished world of this tutorial [here](https://github.com/"
"ignitionrobotics/docs/blob/master/fortress/tutorials/moving_robot/"
"moving_robot.sdf)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:8
msgid "What is a plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:10
msgid ""
"To make our robot move we will use the `diff_drive` plugin. But before doing "
"so let's answer the question \"What is a plugin?\" A plugin is a chunk of "
"code that is compiled as a shared library and inserted into the simulation. "
"Plugins make us control many aspects of the simulation like world, models, "
"etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:12
msgid "Diff_drive plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:14
msgid ""
"`diff_drive` plugin helps us control our robot, specifically a robot that "
"can be differentially driven. Let's setup the plugin on our robot. Open the "
"`building_robot.sdf` and add the following code within the `vehicle_blue` "
"model tags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:19
msgid ""
"<plugin\n"
"    filename=\"libignition-gazebo-diff-drive-system.so\"\n"
"    name=\"ignition::gazebo::systems::DiffDrive\">\n"
"    <left_joint>left_wheel_joint</left_joint>\n"
"    <right_joint>right_wheel_joint</right_joint>\n"
"    <wheel_separation>1.2</wheel_separation>\n"
"    <wheel_radius>0.4</wheel_radius>\n"
"    <odom_publish_frequency>1</odom_publish_frequency>\n"
"    <topic>cmd_vel</topic>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:32
msgid ""
"The `<plugin>` tag has two attributes, `filename` which takes the library "
"file name and `name` which takes the name of the plugin. In the "
"`<left_joint>` and `<right_joint>` tags we define the joints which connect "
"the left and the right wheel with the body of the robot, in our case "
"`left_wheel_joint` and `right_wheel_joint`. `<wheel_separation>` takes the "
"distance between the two wheels. Our robot has its `left_wheel` at 0.6 m and "
"the `right_wheel` at -0.6 m in y-axis with respect to the `chassis`, so the "
"`wheel_separation` is 1.2 m. `<wheel_radius>` takes the radius of the wheel "
"which was defined in the `<radius>` tag under the wheel link. "
"`<odom_publish_frequency>` sets the frequency at which the odometry is "
"published at `/model/vehicle_blue/odometry`. `cmd_vel` is the input "
"`<topic>` to the `DiffDrive` plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:39
msgid "Topics and Messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:41
msgid ""
"Now our model is ready. We just need to send commands (messages) to it. "
"These messages will be published (sent) on the `cmd_vel` topic defined above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:44
msgid ""
"A topic is simply a name for grouping a specific set of messages or a "
"particular service. Our model will subscribe (listen) to the messages sent "
"on the `cmd_vel` topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:47
msgid "Launch the robot world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:49 ../../../moving_robot.md:79
#: ../../../moving_robot.md:127
msgid "`ign gazebo building_robot.sdf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:51
msgid "In another terminal let's send a message to to our robot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:53
msgid ""
"`ign topic -t \"/cmd_vel\" -m ignition.msgs.Twist -p \"linear: {x: 0.5}, "
"angular: {z: 0.05}\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:55
msgid "Now you should have your robot moving in the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:57
msgid "**Note:** Don't forget to press the play button in the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:59
msgid ""
"The command specifies the topic to publish to after the `-t` option. After "
"the `-m` we specify the message type. Our robot expects messages of type "
"`Twist` which consists of two components, `linear` and `angular`. After the "
"`-p` option we specify the content (value) of the message: linear speed `x: "
"0.5` and angular speed `z: 0.05`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:64
msgid ""
"**Hint:** You can know what every topic option does using this command: `ign "
"topic -h`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:66
msgid ""
"For more information about `Topics` and `Messages` in Ignition check the "
"[Transport library tutorials](https://gazebosim.org/api/transport/9.0/"
"tutorials.html)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:68
msgid "Moving the robot using the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:70
msgid ""
"Instead of sending messages from the terminal we will send messages using "
"the keyboard keys. To do so we will add two new plugins: `KeyPublisher` and "
"`TriggeredPublisher`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:72 ../../../moving_robot.md:91
msgid "KeyPublisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:74
msgid ""
"`KeyPublisher` is an `ign-gui` plugin that reads the keyboard's keystrokes "
"and sends them on a default topic `/keyboard/keypress`. Let's try this "
"plugin as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:77
msgid "In one terminal type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:81 ../../../moving_robot.md:129
msgid ""
"In the top right corner click on the plugins dropdown list (vertical "
"ellipsis), click the Key Publisher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:83
msgid "In another terminal type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:85 ../../../moving_robot.md:133
msgid "`ign topic -e -t /keyboard/keypress`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:87
msgid ""
"The last command will display all messages sent on `/keyboard/keypress` "
"topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:89
msgid ""
"In the ignition window press different keys and you should see data "
"(numbers) on the terminal where you run the `ign topic -e -t /keyboard/"
"keypress` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:91
msgid "![KeyPublisher](tutorials/moving_robot/keypublisher_data.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:93
msgid ""
"We want to map these keystrokes into messages of type `Twist` and publish "
"them to the `/cmd_vel` topic which our model listens to. The "
"`TriggeredPublisher` plugin will do this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:96
msgid "Triggered Publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:98
msgid ""
"The `TriggeredPublisher` plugin publishes a user specified message on an "
"output topic in response to an input message that matches user specified "
"criteria. Let's add the following code under the `<world>` tag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:101
msgid ""
"<!-- Moving Forward-->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"libignition-gazebo-triggered-publisher-system.so\"\n"
"        name=\"ignition::gazebo::systems::TriggeredPublisher\">\n"
"    <input type=\"ignition.msgs.Int32\" topic=\"/keyboard/keypress\">\n"
"        <match field=\"data\">16777235</match>\n"
"    </input>\n"
"    <output type=\"ignition.msgs.Twist\" topic=\"/cmd_vel\">\n"
"        linear: {x: 0.5}, angular: {z: 0.0}\n"
"    </output>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:114
msgid ""
"This code defines the `triggered-publisher` plugin. It accepts messages of "
"type `ignition.msgs.Int32` on the `/keyboard/keypress` topic and if the "
"value in the `data` field matches `16777235`(Up arrow key) it outputs a "
"`Twist` message on the `cmd_vel` topic with values `x: 0.5`, `z: 0.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:117
msgid ""
"Now launch `building_robot.sdf` then add the Key Publisher plugin and our "
"robot should move forward as we press the Up arrow key &#8593; (make sure "
"you start the simulation by pressing the play button to see the robot move "
"forward after pressing the Up arrow key)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:119
msgid ""
"There is a demo explaining how the [Triggered Publisher](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/gz-sim/blob/ign-gazebo2/tutorials/triggered_publisher.md) works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:121
msgid "Moving using arrow keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:123
msgid ""
"To see what values are sent on the `/keyboard/keypress` topic when pressing "
"the arrows we can use the `--echo` or `-e` option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:125
msgid "Run the model in one terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:131
msgid "In another terminal run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:135
msgid "Start pressing the arrows keys and see what values they give:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:137
msgid "Left &#8592;  : 16777234"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:138
msgid "Up  &#8593;   : 16777235"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:139
msgid "Right &#8594; : 16777236"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:140
msgid "Down &#8595;  : 16777237"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:142
msgid ""
"We will add the `Triggered publisher` plugin for each arrow key. For "
"example, the Down arrow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:145
msgid ""
"<!-- Moving Backward-->\n"
"<plugin filename=\"libignition-gazebo-triggered-publisher-system.so\"\n"
"        name=\"ignition::gazebo::systems::TriggeredPublisher\">\n"
"    <input type=\"ignition.msgs.Int32\" topic=\"/keyboard/keypress\">\n"
"        <match field=\"data\">16777237</match>\n"
"    </input>\n"
"    <output type=\"ignition.msgs.Twist\" topic=\"/cmd_vel\">\n"
"        linear: {x: -0.5}, angular: {z: 0.0}\n"
"    </output>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:158
msgid ""
"Map each arrow (key stroke) with the desired message (movement) as we did "
"with the backward arrow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:160
msgid "Left &#10142; 16777234 &#10142; linear: {x: 0.0}, angular: {z: 0.5}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:161
msgid "Up &#10142; 16777235 &#10142; linear: {x: 0.5}, angular: {z: 0.0}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:162
msgid "Right &#10142; 16777236 &#10142; linear: {x: 0.0}, angular: {z: -0.5}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../moving_robot.md:163
msgid "Down &#10142; 16777237 &#10142; linear: {x: -0.5}, angular: {z: 0.0}"
msgstr ""

